WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.980
A Louisiana judge barred event contracts for 10 days after the Attorney General sued. This

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:13.200
is Prediction Markets Daily, episode 52. Journalism and education never a bet. After that order,

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:19.140
a federal suit against Arkansas, Novig's place in the volume tables, and a kalshi job built

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:25.500
around a video game, then the board, the week's board, and base rates. Liz Morrill filed that case

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.580
on November 12th in Tanja Pahoa Parish in Louisiana's 21st Judicial District,

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.800
and Judge Jeffrey Johnson signed the emergency order the same afternoon

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:41.480
at 348 without hearing the company's first. It is not a finding that the platform's broke state law.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:45.560
It tells the name defendants to stop offering, listing, clearing,

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:51.360
or otherwise facilitating event contracts for anyone in Louisiana unless they hold a state gaming

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:57.940
license, covers contracts tied to sports, elections and awards, and tells them to geofence the state.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:03.960
It runs out after 10 days unless the court extends it. The longer fight, a request for a preliminary

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:10.520
injunction is set for 9 in the morning on November 30. 31 corporate entities are on the petition,

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:16.880
including Calche and affiliates, QCX, which does business as Polymarket US, Robin Hood,

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:25.640
ForkastX, entities tied to Crypto.com, Coinbase, Gemini, Novig, Underdog, IG Group, and ProfitX.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:30.740
Calci had already sued Louisiana officials in federal court on October 23rd.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:36.600
QCX sued on October 27th, and Calci asked that federal court for its own restraining

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.120
order on November 12th.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:41.620
By Thursday evening, that federal request still had no ruling.

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:47.360
RG.org, citing the advocate, said that at seven that evening, people in Louisiana could

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:49.480
still buy event contracts on Kalshi.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:55.280
Kalshi's head of litigation, Jovi Dadaj, wrote that the operation of federally regulated

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:59.240
exchanges is the exclusive province of the federal government, full stop.

00:02:00.202 --> 00:02:03.042
Arkansas is now on the other side of a federal complaint.

00:02:03.642 --> 00:02:07.822
The block and the defiant report that the Justice Department and the Commodity Futures

00:02:07.822 --> 00:02:12.882
trading commission have sued the state to stop enforcement against CalShi after Arkansas

00:02:12.882 --> 00:02:17.222
sued the exchange on November 4th and called it an illegal gambling platform.

00:02:17.802 --> 00:02:20.822
